--- Core game database container maintaining multi-index hash lookup maps across all Kenshi template and instance records (`GameData`). Provides $O(1)$ indexed retrieval by unique integer ID (`gamedataID`), global string ID (`gamedataSID`), category and name (`gamedataCatName`), and category and string ID (`gamedataCatSID`). Serves as base class for `GameDataManager`.
---@class GameDataContainer
--- Factory method instantiating a new `GameData` object of the specified `itemType`, assigning an integer ID and registering it across all multi-index lookup tables.
---@field createNewData fun(self: GameDataContainer, itemType: integer, forceID: string, name: string): GameData|nil
--- Queries `gamedataCatName` for a record matching both category type and user-friendly name.
---@field getDataByName fun(self: GameDataContainer, dataName: string, category: integer): GameData|nil
--- Renames a managed `GameData` object, updating internal category-name lookup hash tables (`gamedataCatName`) to keep indices consistent.
---@field renameData fun(self: GameDataContainer, data: GameData, name: string)
--- Removes a specific `GameData` record from all lookup maps without deleting the underlying object.
---@field removeData fun(self: GameDataContainer, data: GameData)
--- Purges any earlier duplicate records matching the string ID of `dat` across all multi-index containers.
---@field removeDuplicatesOf fun(self: GameDataContainer, data: GameData)
--- Removes and deallocates all records matching the specified `itemType` category.
---@field removeAllDataOfType fun(self: GameDataContainer, itemType: integer)
--- Purges temporary world object instances while retaining static master template records.
---@field clearInstances fun(self: GameDataContainer)
--- Clears all multi-index lookup containers without deallocating the underlying `GameData` objects.
---@field clearButDontDestroy fun(self: GameDataContainer)
--- Clears all multi-index containers while explicitly preserving platoon and squad records.
---@field clearButDontDestroyPlatoons fun(self: GameDataContainer)
--- Completely empties all lookup containers and deallocates every owned `GameData` object, freeing heap memory.
---@field clearAndDestroy fun(self: GameDataContainer)
--- Generates and returns a unique, strictly ascending sequential integer ID (`currentID++`) for indexing newly created `GameData` instances.
---@field getNewID fun(self: GameDataContainer): integer
--- Removes record `dat` from all lookup tables and enqueues it into global deferred destruction kill list (`killList`).
---@field destroyData fun(self: GameDataContainer, data: GameData)
--- Iterates across all loaded records and resolves string ID references into direct cached memory pointers (`GameData*`), accelerating runtime cross-references.
---@field preLoadAllReferencePtrs fun(self: GameDataContainer)
--- Invalidates and clears all cached direct memory pointers across all records, preparing for mod reload or state purging.
---@field clearAllReferencePtrs fun(self: GameDataContainer)
--- Sets the friendly or mod filename string identifier for this container instance.
---@field setName fun(self: GameDataContainer, name: string)
--- Checks whether an incoming record has an ID or string ID collision with existing records, updating pointer tables if resolving mod overrides.
---@field checkForDuplicates fun(self: GameDataContainer, data: GameData)
--- Registers an existing `GameData` object into this container, assigning a string ID if specified, setting `sourceContainer = this`, and inserting into all 4 lookup maps.
---@field addNewData fun(self: GameDataContainer, dataOrList: GameData|Lektor<GameData>, forceID?: string)
--- Performs fast $O(1)$ hash lookup for a record by its unique global string ID (`gamedataSID`).
---@field getData fun(self: GameDataContainer, idOrSID: integer|string, category?: integer): GameData|nil
--- Populates list with all managed records belonging to a specified `itemType` category.
---@field getDataOfType fun(self: GameDataContainer, list: Lektor<GameData>, itemType: integer)
--- Retrieves direct const reference to the internal integer ID lookup map (`gamedataID`).
---@field _getAllData fun(self: GameDataContainer): OgreUnorderedMap<integer, GameData>
--- Loads game data records from a binary or text file, optionally marking records read-only or active file members, returning success status.
---@field loadGameDataReturn fun(self: GameDataContainer, file: string, isActive: boolean, readOnly: boolean, moreData?: lightuserdata): boolean
