--- Autonomous navigation agent and kinematic path follower bridging character locomotion kinematics (`CharMovement`) to Havok AI navigation meshes (`hkaiNavMesh`). Executes string-pulling portal funneling across NavMesh edge corridors (`EdgePathNode`), local obstacle avoidance steering, dynamic obstacle cylinder-sweep collision detection (`EdgeCache`), and water immersion speed damping.
---@class HavokCharacter
--- Sets the agent's spatial position and updates the current NavMesh polygon face key. Marks `positionChanged = true` to force edge cache and spatial partition updates.
---@field setPosition fun(self: HavokCharacter, p: table, key: integer)
--- Retrieves the current world-space position vector of the Havok navigation agent.
---@field getPosition fun(self: HavokCharacter): table
--- Explicitly assigns the linear kinematic velocity vector of the navigation agent.
---@field setVelocity fun(self: HavokCharacter, v: table)
--- Queries the current linear velocity vector of the character.
---@field getVelocity fun(self: HavokCharacter): table
--- Queries the normalized direction vector towards the currently targeted NavMesh edge or intermediate waypoint.
---@field getWaypointDirection fun(self: HavokCharacter): table
--- Queries the actual travel direction vector traversed during the most recent kinematic simulation integration step.
---@field getDirectionMoved fun(self: HavokCharacter): table
--- Applies a speed attenuation multiplier to account for water immersion drag or deep wading resistance.
---@field setWaterModifier fun(self: HavokCharacter, m: number)
--- Toggles manual navigation steering override mode, bypassing autonomous edge-following path logic for direct manual control.
---@field setManualMode fun(self: HavokCharacter, on?: boolean)
--- Configures the desired forward travel speed target for the kinematic steering controller.
---@field setDesiredSpeed fun(self: HavokCharacter, speed: number)
--- Queries high-level character navigation state (IDLE, GOAL_REACHED, FOLLOWING_PATH, or MANUAL).
---@field getState fun(self: HavokCharacter): integer
--- Queries detailed status of active path computation and execution (NONE, COMPLETE, INCOMPLETE, FAILED, WAITING, UPDATING, BROKEN).
---@field getPathState fun(self: HavokCharacter): integer
--- Determines whether the agent is currently positioned on a valid Havok NavMesh polygon face.
---@field isOnNavmesh fun(self: HavokCharacter): boolean
--- Queries the closest valid NavMesh boundary or portal point within a specified maximum radius, optionally taking dynamic building doorways and obstacles into account.
---@field getClosestPoint fun(self: HavokCharacter, target: table, max: number, building: Building): table
--- Dispatches an asynchronous A* pathfinding query request to the Havok navigation generator queue towards a targeted goal coordinate.
---@field requestPath fun(self: HavokCharacter, goal: table, priority: integer)
--- Clears and invalidates active path structures, resetting path state to `NONE` and clearing pending waypoints.
---@field clearPath fun(self: HavokCharacter)
--- Primary per-frame simulation update step for the Havok character. Advances kinematic movement along path, integrates velocity, executes edge collision queries, and updates steering vectors.
---@field update fun(self: HavokCharacter, time: number)
--- Advances the agent along the current polyline path corridor for a given time step, updating current waypoint and triggering portal funneling string-pulling.
---@field moveAlongPath fun(self: HavokCharacter, time: number): boolean
--- Detects and reacts to dynamic agent-agent and agent-obstacle collisions, adjusting local trajectory and triggering avoidance maneuvers.
---@field handleCollision fun(self: HavokCharacter): boolean
--- Invalidates current path progress if matching an invalidated request ID or region ID, forcing path recalculation.
---@field invalidate fun(self: HavokCharacter, rid: integer)
--- Directly queries the current NavMesh polygon face key.
---@field _getFaceKey fun(self: HavokCharacter): integer
--- Applies string-pulling funnel algorithms across shared NavMesh polygon edges, tightening path corners around left or right portal vertices.
---@field pullThroughVertex fun(self: HavokCharacter, side: integer, index: integer): integer
--- Advances the active path traversal index `nextEdge` to the subsequent polygon boundary edge along `currentPath`.
---@field updateNextEdge fun(self: HavokCharacter): integer
--- Resolves edge cases such as agent getting stuck outside NavMesh boundaries, off-mesh fall recovery, or trapped inside dynamic obstacles.
---@field resolveProblems fun(self: HavokCharacter)
--- Evaluates whether the agent has reached the final destination goal point within acceptable spatial tolerance threshold.
---@field atGoal fun(self: HavokCharacter): boolean
--- Queries the entity handle of another character currently colliding with or impeding this agent.
---@field getCollidedCharacter fun(self: HavokCharacter): hand
--- Associates or updates the entity handle (`hand`) referencing the owning character possessing this Havok agent.
---@field setHandle fun(self: HavokCharacter, h: hand)
--- Calculates projected future agent position and steering orientation along the active path corridor over a specified distance horizon.
---@field calculateFuturePosition fun(self: HavokCharacter, distance: number): table
