--- Background worker thread generating and carving NavMesh polygon meshes from raw terrain heightfields, static meshes, and dynamic building obstacle hulls. Integrates Havok AI (`hkaiNavMesh`, `hkaiNavMeshGenerationSettings`) with PhysX collision scenes, orchestrating multi-threaded task queues, building doorway connections, dynamic obstacle excision, and seamless adjacent zone edge stitching.
---@class NavMeshGenerator
--- Queries whether the generator is actively computing a task or has pending jobs remaining in the queue.
---@field isGenerating fun(self: NavMeshGenerator): boolean
--- Primary worker thread procedure. Continuously pops generation tasks from `queue`, executes voxelization, polygon extraction, carving, and stitching, and pushes completed tasks into `done` queue.
---@field threadProc fun(self: NavMeshGenerator): integer
--- Override dispatch for `threadProc`. Primary worker thread procedure. Continuously pops generation tasks from `queue`, executes voxelization, polygon extraction, carving, and stitching, and pushes completed tasks into `done` queue.
---@field _NV_threadProc fun(self: NavMeshGenerator): integer
--- Worker thread execution tick. Processes the next active task from the queue, invoking `generateTaskBT` within a try-catch block to prevent worker thread aborts.
---@field updateBT fun(self: NavMeshGenerator): boolean
--- Dispatches high-level generation task logic on the worker thread based on task type: full zone generation, building splicing, or dynamic obstacle carving.
---@field generateTaskBT fun(self: NavMeshGenerator, task: lightuserdata)
--- Validates construction and demolition states for all buildings involved in the generation task, ensuring destroyed or moved structures are properly excised.
---@field validateBuildingStates fun(self: NavMeshGenerator, task: lightuserdata): integer
--- Carves out dynamic obstacle volumes from an existing Havok NavMesh, cutting polygon edges and creating walkable boundaries around new building footprints.
---@field carve fun(self: NavMeshGenerator, task: lightuserdata): integer
--- Performs localized navmesh splicing, cutting a rectangular sub-region out of an existing navmesh tile and welding a newly generated replacement patch.
---@field splice fun(self: NavMeshGenerator, t: lightuserdata): integer
--- Stitches building interior navmesh floor slabs to exterior ground entrance portals, connecting doorways to the outdoor pathfinding grid.
---@field stitchInterior fun(self: NavMeshGenerator, t: lightuserdata): integer
--- Stitches exterior ground navmesh around building perimeters to surrounding outdoor terrain mesh.
---@field stitchExterior fun(self: NavMeshGenerator, t: lightuserdata): integer
--- Restores Havok AI generation settings back to global engine defaults after a customized building interior or obstacle carving pass.
---@field revertSettings fun(self: NavMeshGenerator)
--- Releases the multi-threaded lock on a task after main thread consumption and deallocates task memory.
---@field unlockTask fun(self: NavMeshGenerator, task: lightuserdata)
--- Checks whether there are any pending or in-progress generation tasks registered for the specified zone.
---@field hasJob fun(self: NavMeshGenerator, zone: ZoneMap): boolean
--- Main thread update tick called from `NavMesh::update`. Retrieves finished tasks from the `done` queue, registers completed `NavInstance` meshes into the world, and initiates adjacent zone border stitching.
---@field update fun(self: NavMeshGenerator)
