--- Sets the static trading settlement identifier (`currentTradeTown`), establishing the municipal jurisdiction governing price markups, legal prohibitions, and contraband checks during merchant bartering.
---@field setTradingTown fun(town: hand)
--- Retrieves the active trading town pointer by resolving the static `currentTradeTown` handle through `HandleManager`.
---@field getTradingTown fun(): Town
--- Clears all active trade partners from the global `traders` map and deallocates map nodes using `Ogre::NedPoolingPolicy`.
---@field clearTradePartners fun()
--- Scans active trade partners to identify the non-player merchant character. Resolves the owner handle of non-player trade partners through `HandleManager`.
---@field getNPCTrader fun(): Character
--- Static query checking whether the active trading session involves financial currency transactions (Cats) rather than free container looting. Returns the NPC entity if selling/buying for money.
---@field isTradingForMoney_static fun(): RootObject
--- Static query checking whether the active trading session involves looting or stealing from an unwilling or unconscious NPC. Returns the victim `RootObject` if items are considered stolen.
---@field isTradingAndStealing_static fun(): RootObject
--- Calculates the dynamic trade price multiplier for the current merchant transaction based on the NPC trader's platoon economy settings (`priceMultWhenITrade`).
---@field getTraderPriceMultiplier fun(): number
--- Checks whether an item picked up from the specified source inventory can be dropped into another inventory or container without requiring payment.
---@field canDropMouseItemWithoutPaying fun(cameFrom: InventoryGUI): boolean
--- Removes an inventory window from the global trade partner map. If any open fencing or confirmation message box is pending, closes it via `ForgottenGUI`.
---@field removeTradePartner fun(_tradewith: InventoryGUI)
--- Registers an inventory window as an active trade partner in the global barter map (`traders`). Configures transaction parameters including whether money exchange is required, whether items can be freely dropped without payment, and whether the partner represents a player character.
---@field addTradePartner fun(_tradewith: InventoryGUI, payment?: boolean, canDrop?: boolean, isPlayer?: boolean, who: hand)
--- Validates whether a locked equipment item (e.g. slave shackles, torture gear) is actively locked on the character. Returns true if the item is equipped and its lock mechanism has a positive difficulty level and is not currently open.
---@field lockedItemCheck fun(item: LockedArmour): boolean
